From: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: ath12k: implement MLO v2 topology association and peer maps

Qualcomm's multi-chip firmware supports a version 2 MLO topology TLV that
describes the adjacent chips for every member of a WSI group. The legacy
TLV only provides a flat chip and link list. This is insufficient for the
firmware to reliably derive the WSI routing topology when real multi-link
traffic starts.

WLAN.WBE.1.6 firmware is paired with the extended WMI_MLO_PEER_ASSOC_PARAMS
layout used by Qualcomm's current TIP driver. The extension was introduced
together with station link reconfiguration, but the structure size itself
is part of the firmware ABI even when none of the optional reconfiguration
fields are used.

The MLO peer map event is firmware's confirmation that the aggregate peer
was installed. Besides the ML peer ID and MLD address, current firmware
supplies the AST index and cache set used by the data path. The driver
currently consumes only the first two values and entirely ignores the
matching MLO peer unmap event.

Merged from:
  332-wifi-ath12k-advertise-MLO-v2-adjacency-topology.patch
  333-wifi-ath12k-align-MLO-peer-assoc-ABI.patch
  334-wifi-ath12k-handle-complete-MLO-peer-map-events.patch

Based on work by:
  JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>

Signed-off-by: JiaY-shi <shi05275@163.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

